        "exampleID": "prepared-conv1d-classifier",
        "sourceResource": "workflow-observations",
        "title": "Explore Conv1d in a classifier",
        "subtitle": "Apply the same small window at each location in an array.",
        "disclosureTitle": "How a shared window creates features",
        "formula": "Multiply the values inside a small window by its learned weights, add the results, and move that same window to the next location.",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A channel is one set of measurements. Conv1d uses 1 spatial direction, with channels before that direction.",
          "Kernel size controls the window size. Stride is the distance between positions; dilation spaces the values inside the window. Padding adds values around the edges according to the chosen policy and mode.",
          "Inspect the input and output shapes, predict one local result, then run the editable classifier. The shared-kernel lesson checks values and how small input and weight changes affect the result.",
          "Groups split channels into independent sets. Input and output channels must divide evenly into the group count. Bias adds a learned starting value per output channel. Settings stay within the documented allocation limits."
        ],
        "buttonTitle": "Open Conv1d classifier",
        "exampleSource": "Sources/KwipMLCore/Conv1dWorkflowExample.swift"
      }
