        "exampleID": "prepared-conv-transpose1d-classifier",
        "sourceResource": "workflow-observations",
        "title": "Explore ConvTranspose1d in a classifier",
        "subtitle": "Spread input values through a shared window and inspect where they land.",
        "disclosureTitle": "How a transposed shared window changes the output",
        "formula": "Each input value contributes through the same learned window. Contributions that reach the same output position are added together.",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Transposed convolution can enlarge an array, but it is not an inverse that reconstructs the original input. Channels hold sets of measurements; the spatial directions describe locations.",
          "Stride controls the spacing between input contributions; dilation spaces the window values. Padding reduces the output extent. Output padding adjusts the output size without adding a border of filled values.",
          "Each output-padding value must be smaller than stride OR dilation in that direction. Only zero padding is supported; output size follows the configured settings rather than a separate dynamic size argument.",
          "Open the editable classifier, inspect input and output tables, and change one setting at a time. The shared-kernel lesson measures values and how small input and weight changes affect results. Groups and bias retain the same channel and allocation rules."
        ],
        "buttonTitle": "Open ConvTranspose1d classifier",
        "exampleSource": "Sources/KwipMLCore/ConvTranspose1dWorkflowExample.swift"
      }
